.TH "WARP\-UNINSTALL" "1" "" "warp" "warp Manual"
.SH "NAME"
warp\-uninstall \- report how to remove this warp installation
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B warp uninstall
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Prints how to remove this installation of warp, chosen from how the running executable was installed: the owning package manager's own removal command where one owns it, and the path to delete otherwise.
.PP
Deliberately reports rather than removes. Deleting files a package manager owns leaves that manager's database inconsistent, and a command that deletes its own executable cannot report what happened if the deletion half\-succeeds.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
The command completed successfully.
.TP
\fB1\fR
The command failed. The reason is reported on standard error.
.TP
\fB2\fR
The command was invoked incorrectly (missing or invalid arguments).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR warp (1),
.BR warp\-upgrade (1)
